    "2": {
      "uid": 2,
      "key": [
        "Khorramdin",
        "Brass Mask",
        "Shiruyeh",
        "brass-masked king"
      ],
      "keysecondary": [
        "Gurabad"
      ],
      "comment": "Parvezravan: Khorramdin and the Brass Mask",
      "content": "Shiruyeh ('unweaned lion cub') was banished by his father, wore a brass mask and called himself Khorramdin. He promised justice to slaves and commoners as an emissary of Nabu Malikata; Liloupar supported him and the revolt she fuelled led to the Great Revolt and Gurabad's fall. The Tale says he later fell into the chasm in the earth; Liloupar calls him a gifted charlatan who led followers to their doom. His plague is called Shiruyeh's Plague.",
