      "comment": "Parvezravan: Spirit of Victory",
      "content": "The epithet comes from Kisra's conquests. The Tale credits him with ninety-nine cities, tribes and sages, and records of his reign use it in his name when conscripting workers and building pleasure gardens, workshops and fortified camps.",
